  "body": "### What are you trying to do\n\nWhat is the best way to onboard a new machine?\n\nWe probably should gather the basic information:\n- name of the machine\n- type of machine (milling, turning, etc.)\n- type of post processor\n- limits of x, y, z, a, b, c, etc.\n- spindle speed ranges\n\nDo we want to keep a copy of the machine's operational guide/documentation? (for machine specifics like M codes)\n\n### How you imagine it working\n\nAs a developer/contributor, what info do we need to enable a new machine?\n\nWhat code examples would we want a new machine user to run to validate the machine?\n\nDo we want to have some example models (step files for now?) that have most of the basic operations? \n\nmilling: face, contour, slot, pocket, chamfer, drilling, boring, tapping\nturning: face, turn, groove, knurl, tapping, threading\n",
